WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.336
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.438
We hope you're doing well, and
now we're gonna get to the news.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:08.240
President Biden held a virtual
meeting today with

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.109
Russian president
Vladimir Putin,

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:12.178
though it was weird
that they decided to do it

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:14.247 line:0%
in the metaverse.

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:17.550
According to a new book,

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.753
hours after former president
Trump announced, in 2020,

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:23.122
that he had tested positive
for the coronavirus,

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:25.024
his health deteriorated
very quickly.

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:27.927
They kept him alive by
immediately hooking him up

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.296
to a camera and a microphone.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:32.899
Senate Majority Leader --

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:36.069
[ As Trump ] That's my oxygen.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.704
Senate Majority Leader
Chuck Schumer

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.507
yesterday reiterated
his goal for Democrats

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:43.309
to pass the Build Back Better
spending Bill by Christmas,

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:49.882
the same night Joe Manchin will
be visited by three spirits.

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:52.451
New York governor Kathy Hochul
announced yesterday

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:55.221
that there are a total of
12 confirmed cases

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:58.424
of the Omicron variant of the
coronavirus across the state.

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:02.195
That story again --
There are 12,000 cases

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:05.231
of the Omicron variant in
New York state.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:08.768
"We got 12.
We're sure that's it."

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:11.570
The fifth annual gingerbread
replica of The Capitol

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:12.939
made its debut yesterday,

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.340
but, sadly,
it's just been breached.

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:23.216
You know what?

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:27.419
He's so lovable,
you're still rooting for him.

00:01:27.419 --> 00:01:29.722
During a new interview,
billionaire Elon Musk

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.158
said that his Neuralink company
hopes to start

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:35.394
implanting brain chips in humans
sometime next year.

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:38.497
Kind of intriguing, but I don't
think I'd get the first one.

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:41.067
I mean, you remember
the iPhone 1?

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.802
Exactly, you know?

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.704
You get the first chip,
and in three years,

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.105
everybody will be,
like, making fun of you.

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:48.608
"You got the 1?

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:51.878
Can you even watch
TikToks with that?"

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:55.048
Today was Maine Senator
Susan Collins' 69th birthday,

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:58.551
though she's confident
that she will remain 68.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.587
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.860
They all left?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.230
Trump Tower recently
began selling a cocktail

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.900
inspired by former president
Trump called 45,

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.636
and it secretly reports to
a white Russian.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.671
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.745
That really hammers home
how the last joke did.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.681
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.984
"Maybe it's them. Oh, it's not."

00:02:32.651 --> 00:02:34.821
More than 30 people
recently spent the night

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:37.323
at an IKEA in Denmark
after a snowstorm

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.657
stranded them at the store.

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:40.426
And then they were
stranded another night

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.829
because they couldn't
find the exit.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.564
And I didn't know this,
but in Denmark,

00:02:45.564 --> 00:02:47.734
all their furniture
has normal names.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.769
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.442
It was announced today that
investment manager Peter Lynch

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:59.045
will donate more than
$20 million worth of art

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:02.014
to his alma mater,
Boston College's, art museum.

00:03:02.014 --> 00:03:04.183
Lynch hopes the donation
will help Bostonians

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:07.220
learn to correctly pronounce
the word "art."

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.756
"No, that's aht.

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:13.626
That's aht, bro."

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:15.495
And, finally,
Instagram today launched

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:17.729
a so-called "Take a Break" tool.

00:03:17.729 --> 00:03:20.299
A break from Instagram,
or as its otherwise called,

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:22.034
Twitter.

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:23.403
And that was the monologue,
everybody!

